/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate29_vp_methylTertPentylEther -- the vapour pressure of methylTertPentylEther, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  methylTertPentylEther`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je101250d                21 pts  313.44-359.95 K  Mejia; Segura; Cartes
      10.1021/je0255980                11 pts  274.2-307.8 K  Verevkin; Krasnykh; Vasiltsova; Heintz
      10.1021/je049867t                11 pts  298.02-355.64 K  Vorenberg; Raal; Ramjugernath
      10.1021/je901026b                 5 pts  318.13-338.28 K  Bernatova; Pavlicek; Wichterle
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.06.017: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.10.024: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je200215d: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C283, Vitor 2026-11-10, declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  the DEFAULT of C283: ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed
  false) when the maximum relative P error over all kept points is at most
  5 % and the normal-boiling-point condition below holds with an
  absolute error below 1 K.  This case declares no
  `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case that needs another
  acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The AmbroseWalton curve's
  errors on the same points are reported beside the fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 359.51 K is judged against the range of the KEPT points (all studies span 274.2-359.95 K before any outlier is discarded): if Tb lies OUTSIDE that range, the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within the acceptance's temperature error of it, or the gap is announced and the fit is not promoted; inside it, the gap is reported and is not a condition.

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.240937 - 1366.2891/(T + -36.8588),
  in-sample R2 0.999996 over 21 points, 313.44-359.95 K. HELD OUT: 11
  points, AAD 9.9414 % against the band 7.8 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 359.46 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 9.941 % against the band 7.8 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton THEN C281 step 3,
  objective twoStage, one study fitted and one held out, judged by the
  band (superseded by C283): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`;
  measured, not argued). Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) =
  4.153458 - 1314.0100/(T + -42.6484), in-sample R2 0.999991 over 21
  points, 313.44-359.95 K. HELD OUT: 11 points, AAD 9.1421 % (max 13.3936
  %) against the band 7.8 % -> notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares
  answer on the same points: AAD 9.9414 %, max 14.6229 %. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 359.45 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 9.142 % against the band 7.8 % declared before the
  fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
